{
  "dom_id": "step-35193",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Naming a Given Platonic Solid",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268510/assets/8f545282537781d088d76c2b73e387ebcc7cddaa6e518d9cb2b4f6fa263da024.png)\n\nWhat regular polyhedron is shown in the picture above?\n\nI. Dodecahedron\n\nII. Icosahedron\n\nIII. Tetrahedron",
  "worked_solution": "The picture shows a *tetrahedron*, a convex regular polyhedron that  \n\n- consists of $4$ congruent faces, each in the form of an equilateral triangle, and\n\n- exactly $3$ faces meet at each vertex.\n\nRecall that there are only five types of Platonic solids (convex regular polyhedra):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268510/assets/bc67deabe1622e7ac3015c3ec942f254e59c58f406e026c367e0c0aeee5a6d3e.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-35193\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"35193\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"9402\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-35193\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-10\">Naming a Given Platonic Solid</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"35193\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <div id=\"graphic-b79fdcb7e892d49f01b5ef3ecb3c0d04\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/b79fdcb7e892d49f01b5ef3ecb3c0d04\"></div>\n\n<p>What regular polyhedron is shown in the picture above?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\">\n<li>  Dodecahedron </li>\n<li>  Icosahedron </li>\n<li>  Tetrahedron </li>\n</ol>\n            </div>     \n\n            <div class=\"explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div>\n\n            <div class=\"exampleExplanation\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>The picture shows a <em>tetrahedron</em>, a convex regular polyhedron that  </p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>consists of <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.162ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 500.5 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">4</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E1-MJMAIN-34\" d=\"M462 0Q444 3 333 3Q217 3 199 0H190V46H221Q241 46 248 46T265 48T279 53T286 61Q287 63 287 115V165H28V211L179 442Q332 674 334 675Q336 677 355 677H373L379 671V211H471V165H379V114Q379 73 379 66T385 54Q393 47 442 46H471V0H462ZM293 211V545L74 212L183 211H293Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAIN-34\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> congruent faces, each in the form of an equilateral triangle, and</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>exactly <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.162ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 500.5 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-2-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-2-Title\">3</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E2-MJMAIN-33\" d=\"M127 463Q100 463 85 480T69 524Q69 579 117 622T233 665Q268 665 277 664Q351 652 390 611T430 522Q430 470 396 421T302 350L299 348Q299 347 308 345T337 336T375 315Q457 262 457 175Q457 96 395 37T238 -22Q158 -22 100 21T42 130Q42 158 60 175T105 193Q133 193 151 175T169 130Q169 119 166 110T159 94T148 82T136 74T126 70T118 67L114 66Q165 21 238 21Q293 21 321 74Q338 107 338 175V195Q338 290 274 322Q259 328 213 329L171 330L168 332Q166 335 166 348Q166 366 174 366Q202 366 232 371Q266 376 294 413T322 525V533Q322 590 287 612Q265 626 240 626Q208 626 181 615T143 592T132 580H135Q138 579 143 578T153 573T165 566T175 555T183 540T186 520Q186 498 172 481T127 463Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-33\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> faces meet at each vertex.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Recall that there are only five types of Platonic solids (convex regular polyhedra):</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-6709219b32bcd63fc10ba6f10ea1a953\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/6709219b32bcd63fc10ba6f10ea1a953\"></div> \n\n            </div>           \n        </div>",
